    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.surround\n\n### Description\n\nHello,\n\nWhile looking at the code I realized there may be no way for to automatically map a key to delete a block?\nIt looks like the [delete function here](\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.surround/blob/1a2b59c77a0c4713a5bd8972da322f842f4821b1/lua/mini/surround.lua#L803) takes no arguments.\n\n\nIt would be nice to automatically delete, replace, add etc... a block/string.. like this given an argument:\n\n```lua\n        keys = {\n            {\n                mode = { \"n\", \"v\" },\n                \"<C-,>\",\n                function() require(\"mini.surround\").delete(\"block\") end,\n                desc = \"Delete Surround Block\",\n            },\n        },\n```\n\nAlthough I don't use emacs much these days I'm mostly wanting to reproduce what [smartparens](https://github.com/Fuco1/smartparens) does with `sp-unwrap-sexp`.\n\nThanks",
