            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Hi!\n\n> It would be nice to automatically delete, replace, add etc... a block/string.. like this given an argument:\n\nThe suggested way is to use provided operator `sa`  and actions `sd` / `sr` directly. If by \"block\" you mean [any of three parenthesis](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/48f48e4b3f317e9da34ee7a01958b4c5018e2d34/doc/mini-surround.txt#L177-L178), then it is `sdb` to delete, `srb`+<surrounding id to replace with> to replace, and `sa` + <textobject/motion> + `surrounding id to add` to add.\n\nIf you want a more concise mapping for some common actions, then mapping directly to keys should work. Something like this:\n\n```lua\nvim.keymap.set({ 'n', 'x' }, '<C-,>', 'sdb', { remap = true })\n```\n\nDoes this solve the problem?",
