        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "@echasnovski  I did try 'sdb' but for some reason it inputs 'bd'. I think this is\nbecause the way [Lazy Key Mappings](https://lazy.folke.io/spec/lazy_loading#%EF%B8%8F-lazy-key-mappings) handle the second argument. I'm not going to use lazy keys with `normal` or feedkeys. Instead going to use your vanilla suggestion\nat the end of my config and call it done.  Closing this since the vanilla solution works. Thanks for your help.\n\n```lua\n    {\n        \"echasnovski/mini.surround\",\n        event = \"VeryLazy\",\n        -- No need to copy this inside `setup()`. Will be used automatically.\n        config = function(_, opts)\n            opts = {\n                -- ... .. ...\n            }\n            require(\"mini.surround\").setup(opts)\n            -- after calling require('mini.surround').setup()\n            -- vim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<C-,>\", \"sdb\", { desc = \"Surround: sdb\", silent = true })\n            vim.keymap.set({ \"n\", \"x\" }, \"<C-,>\", \"sdb\", { remap = true })\n        end,\n\n        keys = {\n            {\n                \"<leader>ww\",\n                \"normal! sbd\",\n                { remap = true, mode = { \"n\", \"x\" }, remap = true },\n            },\n        },\n    },\n```",
