            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "It is a bit weird how if I delay till which-key opens it changes mini.surround behaves or maybe\na timeout on the operator. For example with this mapping:\n\n```lua\n            vim.keymap.set( {\"n\", \"x\" }, \"sab\", \"sa%\", { remap = true, desc = \"Surround with ()[]{}\" }\n```\n\nIf I do `sabl` fast before which-key comes up it works as expected. However, if I wait for which-key, it will do\nsomething else.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c3f87cd1-f436-4896-9dcc-f32e632160b5)\n\n\n",
